# Cross-repo API contracts

Backend (`fastapi-backend`) and this app are separate git roots. Contract drift is a common failure mode.

## When backend response/request shapes change

- Update `src/types/*` and the matching `src/api/*` module in the same frontend PR/initiative
- Align status enums carefully (`complete` vs `completed`, Role values)
- Extend Playwright route mocks (`mockDirectorSession` / event mocks) so smoke e2e still matches
- Prefer additive fields; treat removed/renamed fields as breaking and search for callers

## Errors

- UI continues to use `getErrorMessage` — do not parse ad-hoc shapes that diverge from backend `build_error_body`

## Do not

- Leave `Record<string, any>` / `type_config: any` as the long-term contract for new features — narrow types as the feature stabilizes

## Dual-engine / retired endpoints

When the backend retires process/calculate routes in favor of live standings GETs:

1. Delete unused frontend clients in the same change (do not leave methods that hit 410)
2. Point UI at standings/report GETs/POSTs only
3. Keep client math mirrors (`eliminatorProjection`, fund helpers) tested against backend examples so list previews match reports
